- **Concern**: The plan adds a new `python-pyright` workflow job but does not register it in the hard-coded CI failure surfaces: `scripts/ci-failed-jobs.sh` / `scripts/test-ci-failed-jobs.sh`, `python/config.py` `CI_FIXABLE_JOBS`, and `python/ci_monitor.py` `per_job_command` / `prepare_python_toolchain` (with downstream impact on `python/ci_agentic_fix.py`). Today pyright failures are fixable under `python-lint` → `make py-lint`. After the split, pyright-only failures land on an unmapped job name. Two failure modes follow: (1) `make test-ci-failed-jobs` / harness lint fails with `workflow job missing from ci-failed-jobs mapping: python-pyright`; (2) `/implement --merge` CI-fix classifies `python-pyright` as no-local-equivalent and bails before the agentic fixer runs.
